s; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Colorado sits in the 2028 presidential race as an open contest, with the incumbent Republican president term-limited and no nominee settled on either side. The state's recent fundamentals favor Democrats by about six points, and that structural lean is the main quantitative anchor for this forecast, since no general-election polls, expert ratings, or market prices are yet available.\n\nHeadlines add texture but little precision. Democratic primary voters have delivered progressive upsets in Colorado, which could shape the nominee and the party's general-election positioning, while national polling shows mixed 2028 matchups. Until candidates and polling emerge, the race stays rated as a Democratic lean with wide uncertainty, and it could tighten or widen quickly once the field is known.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7597, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6966, "margin": 5.5}]}